  "title": "A terrible secret",
  "section": "Movie Facts # 8 of 10",
  "description": "Sometime during the Hoth scenes of The Empire Strikes Back, it's discovered that R2-D2's beeping noises attract local wampas, an idea inspired by the famous \"Pied Piper\" fairy tale. Artoo leads these furry predators into a large room and the Rebels then place a red and yellow warning sign on the door so their fellow freedom fighters won't wander into the place and wind up wampa lunch. This sequence with R2-D2 was apparently filmed, but never made it into the final cut. A short while later, while on their way to the medical center to visit Luke, Artoo and C-3PO pass by the wampa pen and briefly discuss the ongoing threat these abominable snow beasts pose."
}
